{"name":"Myself","hex":"#8e6f76","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Myself","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of myself used when speaking as God or another important figure who is understood from context."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Myself"}],"entries":[{"title":"Myself (Jolin Tsai album)","blocks":[{"text":"Myself is the eleventh studio album by Taiwanese singer Jolin Tsai, released on August 13, 2010, by Warner. Centered around the theme of partying, the album features a strong emphasis on dance music, which makes up 80% of its content. It was produced by Adia, Paula Ma, and Andrew Chen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Jolin_myself.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myself_(Jolin_Tsai_album)","wikidata":"Q710981"},{"title":"Myself (August Alsina album)","blocks":[{"text":"Myself is the fourth studio album by American singer and songwriter August Alsina. It was released on March 10, 2023, through his label Shake the World and Empire Distribution. It features guest appearances by 4ayem, Deeno., Layton Greene and Zu. Production was handled by several producers including long time collaborators The Exclusives."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/August_Alsina_Myself.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myself_(August_Alsina_album)","wikidata":"Q123134393"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Jolin_myself.jpg/250px-Jolin_myself.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Jolin_myself.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Jolin_myself.jpg/250px-Jol